1
00:00:18,370 --> 00:00:21,000
OK, Richard. That's terrific.

2
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,900
Your pressure is 120 over 75, and that's fine.

3
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:36,280
Now stand up, please.

4
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:41,040
Good, it's 122 over 80.

5
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:45,700
You can sit down now.

6
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:48,490
When was your last complete physical?

7
00:00:48,490 --> 00:00:49,880
Six months ago.

8
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:52,110
Good. Do you have any back or knee problems?

9
00:00:52,110 --> 00:00:54,880
Nope. I am in perfect health.

10
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:56,520
What do you do for a living, Mr. Stewart?

11
00:00:56,520 --> 00:00:57,880
I'm a photographer.

12
00:00:57,880 --> 00:01:00,280
Interesting. What do you photograph?

13
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:05,950
Everything. The American scene. People, places, events.

14
00:01:05,950 --> 00:01:10,060
Did you ever think of photographing an aerobics class?

15
00:01:10,060 --> 00:01:14,890
No...I can't remember taking pictures of people exercising.

16
00:01:14,890 --> 00:01:16,750
But don't you think it'd be a good subject?

17
00:01:16,750 --> 00:01:20,490
Sure.

18
00:01:20,490 --> 00:01:23,510
I need some good photos for my advertising, Mr. Stewart.

19
00:01:23,510 --> 00:01:25,080
Maybe you can photogragh a class,

20
00:01:25,080 --> 00:01:27,070
and I can give you and Mrs.Stewart

21
00:01:27,070 --> 00:01:28,870
a month of classes ree.

22
00:01:28,870 --> 00:01:30,490
When can I photograph a class?

23
00:01:30,490 --> 00:01:32,520
Anytime.

24
00:01:32,520 --> 00:01:33,540
How about today?

25
00:01:33,540 --> 00:01:37,070
Terrific!

26
00:01:37,070 --> 00:01:39,360
Hi.

27
00:01:39,360 --> 00:01:43,660
Oh, hi.

28
00:01:43,660 --> 00:01:44,090
Are we ready to go?

29
00:01:44,090 --> 00:01:44,640
Yeah. Yeah. Let's get in our lines.

30
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:48,300
We're going to take it slow first.

31
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:50,190
Stretch up...and we're going to go left first ...

32
00:01:50,190 --> 00:02:03,000
2,3,4 ... now switch. ...

33
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,880
OK, hold to the right.

34
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:13,250
Sunrises. Stretch it out. Flat back.

35
00:02:13,250 --> 00:02:27,180
Bring it up ... and twists ... and side ... 2, 3 ...

36
00:02:27,180 --> 00:02:35,700
and left ... push ... push ... turn ... hit the floor.

37
00:02:35,700 --> 00:02:50,770
Take it side again .... OK, and switch. Stretch it out.

38
00:02:50,770 --> 00:02:54,090
And we're going to warm down with a tango.

39
00:02:54,090 --> 00:03:11,860
Left, right. Enjoy it.

40
00:03:11,860 --> 00:03:14,550
Richard, did you go to the Davis Aerobics class today?

41
00:03:14,550 --> 00:03:20,150
Yes, I went to the aerobics class today.

42
00:03:20,150 --> 00:03:23,120
What is wrong with you?

43
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:25,720
Nothing. I am in excellent health.

44
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:29,020
I have ideal blood pressure. A perfect heart.

45
00:03:29,020 --> 00:03:33,880
In other words, I'm in wonderful condition.

46
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:36,670
Richard, did you go to the aerobics class, really?

47
00:03:36,670 --> 00:03:40,750
And don't forget to invite Susan for dinner.

48
00:03:40,750 --> 00:03:42,410
And your legs don't hurt?

49
00:03:42,410 --> 00:03:46,210
Hurt? What do you mean?

50
00:03:46,210 --> 00:03:50,600
What about your arms? Lift your arms up like this.

51
00:03:50,600 --> 00:03:54,320
And they don't hurt ot even a little?

52
00:03:54,320 --> 00:03:58,630
Nope.

53
00:03:58,630 --> 00:04:01,630
You are in great condition. I can't believe it!
